  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14180007/assets/bea8536b726a48046b995d180bd9136146d491721a9197f696c7a5e9af43a6ba.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅=\\{\\},\\,\\{x\\},\\,\\{y\\},\\,\\{x,y\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)=\\{∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{x,y\\}\\}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
